#: ../../udapp.rst:11
msgid "Interacting with deployed contracts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../udapp.rst:13
msgid "After you deploy a contract or :ref:`load it into Remix using Add Contract <run:loading deployed contracts>`, the deployed instance will appear in the **Deployed Contracts** section on Deploy & Run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../udapp.rst:15
msgid "Deployed Instances"
msgstr ""

#: ../../udapp.rst:18
msgid "The deployed contract's address is visible as are a few other icons - one of which is the **pin** icon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../udapp.rst:21
msgid "Pinned contracts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../udapp.rst:23
msgid "When a contract is pinned, its address and ABI are stored in the ``.deploys`` folder of the current Workspace. Upon reloading Remix, pinned contracts will automatically appear in the **Deployed Contracts** section, provided that both the Workspace and the connected blockchain network remain the same as when the contract was originally pinned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../udapp.rst:26
msgid "Functions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../udapp.rst:28
msgid "To see a contract's functions, click on the deployed contract."
msgstr ""

#: ../../udapp.rst:38
msgid "The functions' buttons can have different colors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../udapp.rst:40
msgid "Blue buttons are for ``view`` or ``pure`` functions. Clicking a blue button does not create a new transaction - so there will be **no gas fees**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../udapp.rst:42
msgid "Orange buttons are for ``non-payable`` functions. Non-payable functions change the state of the contract BUT **do not accept value** (typically ETH) being sent with the transaction. Clicking an orange button will create a transaction and will cost gas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../udapp.rst:44
msgid "Red buttons are for ``payable`` functions. Clicking a red button will create a new transaction and this transaction can accept a **value** (typically ETH). The amount of value is set in the **Value** field which is under the Gas Limit field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../udapp.rst:46
msgid "Calling different function types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../udapp.rst:50
msgid "Inputting parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../udapp.rst:52
msgid "A function has two views - the collapsed and the expanded view. Clicking the function brings you to the expanded view, where you can input the parameters required for the function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../udapp.rst:54
msgid "The input box shows the expected type of each parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../udapp.rst:55
msgid "Numbers and addresses do not need to be wrapped in double quotes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../udapp.rst:56
msgid "Strings must be wrapped in double quotes."
msgstr ""

